From: AshesTom <258768419+AshesTom@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] win32u, winex11: send what a window draws inside another process's window

Purpose: XP Explorer's recent programs (startmenu-view.exe, a child of
explorer's pinned list in the Start menu) highlight under the pointer at
once, as the Start menu's own items do.
Windows behavior: what a window paints is on the screen when its paint
ends, whichever process owns its parent.
Wine before: a window inside another process's top-level window has no
window surface in its own process; its DC draws on gdi_display straight
into that top-level's X window. The thread flushes its surfaces before it
waits, which leaves that drawing out, and since 0039 creating a memory DC
no longer flushes the display. The highlight stayed in the X buffer until
an unrelated request flushed it: the XQueryPointer of TrackMouseEvent's
timer, 400 ms later, or the next item's paint (the highlight followed the
pointer one item behind).
Change: with the opt-in, releasing the DC of a window whose top-level
window belongs to another process sends it FLUSHOUTPUT, the escape that
asks a device for the output it holds; winex11 flushes gdi_display.
Evidence: in the nested X11 session, the time from a pointer move to the
highlight of a recent program on the screen went from 400-800 ms to 5 ms,
the same as the pinned Internet item (Xephyr, 1024x768, Olive Green).
Scope: WIN4WINE_EXTERNAL_SHELL.
---
diff --git a/dlls/win32u/dce.c b/dlls/win32u/dce.c
--- a/dlls/win32u/dce.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/dce.c
@@ -1252,6 +1252,19 @@
 
     TRACE( "%p %p\n", hwnd, hdc );
 
+    /* win4wine: a window inside another process's top-level window has no
+     * surface in this process, so the thread flushes nothing that it drew
+     * before it waits. Have the driver send it, with the escape that asks a
+     * device for the output it holds. */
+    if (hwnd && win4wine_external_shell())
+    {
+        HWND top = NtUserGetAncestor( hwnd, GA_ROOT );
+        WND *win = top ? get_win_ptr( top ) : NULL;
+
+        if (win == WND_OTHER_PROCESS) NtGdiExtEscape( hdc, NULL, 0, FLUSHOUTPUT, 0, NULL, 0, NULL );
+        else if (win && win != WND_DESKTOP) release_win_ptr( win );
+    }
+
     user_lock();
     dce = get_dc_dce( hdc );
     if (dce && dce->count && dce->hwnd)
diff --git a/dlls/winex11.drv/init.c b/dlls/winex11.drv/init.c
--- a/dlls/winex11.drv/init.c
+++ b/dlls/winex11.drv/init.c
@@ -530,6 +530,15 @@
         }
         break;
 
+    case FLUSHOUTPUT:
+        /* win4wine: win32u sends it when a DC of a window inside another
+         * process's window is released. Such a DC draws on gdi_display
+         * straight into that X window, and since 0039 no memory DC flushes
+         * the display: what it drew waited for an unrelated request. */
+        if (!win4wine_external_shell()) break;
+        XFlush( gdi_display );
+        return TRUE;
+
     case X11DRV_ESCAPE:
         if (in_data && in_count >= sizeof(enum x11drv_escape_codes))
         {
